27. So far as the offence punishable under Section 171G is concerned, the same envisages punishment for false statement in connection with an election and the ingredients of the said offence are:-
 (i) An election was impending;
 (ii) The accused made a public statement relating to the personal character and conduct of the candidate;
(iii) Such statement was false to the knowledge to the accused or accused believed that it was false or that he did not believe it to be true;
(iv) The accused published the statement with intent to affect his result of the election.

